This product implements the BBC TAMS API specification and includes it
as a git submodule under src/vendor/bbc-tams/.

This distribution does not contain that upstream git submodule; it vendors the
frozen `assets/openapi.json` contract and SQL/migration provenance described
below.

Modification notice (2026-08-20): Livewyer Ltd rewrote the API, worker, health,
and migration runtime in Rust; added the static Alpine multi-architecture image,
operator-compatible argv dispatcher, conformance/validation scripts, and
operational rollback documentation; and retained the frozen contract and SQL
migration assets with their upstream provenance. `assets/openapi.json` is the
unchanged frozen packaged BBC contract; runtime code changes only its three
advertised version fields in memory. Dependency licenses are reported by the
repository's cargo-deny/source-archive inventory.

TASM modification notice (2026-09-18):
The Rust HTTP handlers, domain models, PostgreSQL repositories and background
jobs have been adapted from rust-tams-api commit
58c73d8add60a819605c1009661872f676c2769d for browser WebAssembly execution.
Native server, authentication, console and infrastructure components are omitted.
The PostgreSQL adapter uses PGlite, and browser storage uses IndexedDB and OPFS.
Timestamp arithmetic and encoded object identity handling have been changed.

Canonical JSON code is adapted from the ibc-cnm-demo-1 workspace, licensed
under Apache-2.0 (git base 56f6986e56407d26938bde90011e0e23a3cd3907).
The exact source file hash is recorded in contracts/provenance.json.
The TAMS 8.2 API specification and documentation are vendored in contracts/tams/
at commit 34fb31b80cb8afb3194f28c8b787301379caacf8. The notices above describe
upstream distributions; paths in this distribution are listed in
contracts/provenance.json.

